 ('TX-001','When two people book the same room.','DATABASE INTEGRITY','Race conditions are product bugs. A booking UI alone cannot guarantee an available slot.','Enforce non-overlapping time ranges where concurrent requests meet: the database.','#73F6DC','#4777ED',['PostgreSQL exclusion constraint blocks conflicting intervals.','Back-to-back bookings remain valid.','Data integrity—not only frontend validation.'],'cowork'),
 ('TX-002','The last seat should have only one owner.','CONCURRENT SYSTEMS','Two simultaneous ride requests must never reserve the same final seat.','Use ordered database row locks inside one transaction to make acceptance atomic.','#FFBB79','#FE548A',['Lock rows in a consistent order.','Calculate fare changes in integer poysha.','421 passing tests across API, web and database.'],'tesla'),
